__pycache__
*.o
build
cmake/sys.cmake.ext
output*
*.png
*.dat
*.txt
*.data
*.vtp
*.sav*
*.new*
*.old*
*_results

# nsys profiling artifacts: the report and the sqlite export nsys stats
# generates from it. Tens of MB a run, and reproducible from the commands
# in tests/unit_tests/test1_node_force/bench_segseg_force.py
*.nsys-rep
*.sqlite

# editor settings, personal to whoever is working here
.vscode/

!CMakeLists.txt

# input_data/ and ref_data/ hold test fixtures, not simulation output. Anything
# under them is a committed input to the test suite rather than something a run
# produces, whatever its extension. Without these the *.dat fixtures are
# swallowed by the blanket *.dat above and a fresh clone cannot run the tests.
!tests/*/*/input_data/*.dat
!tests/*/*/ref_data/*.dat

# paradis_default.data is a committed input deck for examples/06_paradis, not
# something a run produces, so it must survive the blanket *.data above.
!examples/06_paradis/*.data
